<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="AYNI" pubkey="" timestamp="1782076632" url="https://wie-utp.github.io/ayni-releases/repo" version="20002"><description>Official release channel for AYNI, the offline AI support app for children with autism spectrum disorder. A project of WIE UTP and IEEE EPICS.</description></repo><application id="com.ayni.ayni"><id>com.ayni.ayni</id><added>2026-06-21</added><lastupdated>2026-06-21</lastupdated><name>AYNI</name><summary>Offline AI support for children with ASD</summary><desc>AYNI (reciprocity in Quechua) is a fully offline Android tablet app that gives
behavioral support to children with autism spectrum disorder, plus a
psychoeducational guide for parents and educators.

Everything runs on the device. No internet, no cloud, no child data ever
leaving the tablet.

* Four calm, predictable mini-games designed with the TEACCH method
* A parent and educator Q&amp;A grounded in a clinician-authored knowledge base
* A therapist panel with anonymized, opt-in engagement data

Built for therapy centers in low-connectivity communities in Peru. A project
of the WIE Student Branch at Universidad Tecnologica del Peru, funded by
